# C30 remediation after attempt-01 (7/6/6/6/6, fail)

| Finding | Remediation | Where |
|---|---|---|
| R1 wizard completion bypassed the switch guard | `completeTenantSetup` gained `resolution?` and runs through `guard_switch` before anything is committed or retired: a pending decision refuses it with `switchBlocked{to: <draft id>, completion: true}`; the draft, the active tenant and the approval stay; the wizard renders the one guard dialog (portalled above the sheet) and re-sends the completion with the resolution. Tests: `harness_tools::completing_a_tenant_setup_is_the_guarded_switch_path` (real engine, real pending approval), `wizard.test` completion guard | `authority.rs`, `setup_domain.rs` (`completable_setup`), `inbox_domain.rs`, `wizard.tsx`, `switch-guard.tsx` |
| R2 Discard kept the transcript | `discard_harness` records the conversation's scope and history id as discarded: `admit_history_write` refuses every later save of it (the cut-short turn), and a `HistoryJob::Discard` removes its record under the same lock the sink holds (so a save under way finishes first) and refreshes the listing. Test: `harness_tools::discard_removes_the_saved_transcript_and_archive_keeps_it` (a saved earlier turn plus a pending turn; archive keeps, discard removes, listed after switching back) | `harness_domain.rs`, `harness_history.rs` |
| R3 one context-bound overview and global bookkeeping | Each opened tenant owns an `OverviewRecord` (last read, the other products' outcomes, in-flight parts, generation, recheck, snooze receipt) for the session; a switch away and back shows it again without a new read; a reply admitted under a retired context is withdrawn and never recorded (and counts no completion). Tests: `ui_v2_inbox::a_tenants_read_survives_a_switch_away_and_back_without_a_new_read` | `observation_domain.rs`, `inbox_domain.rs` |
| R4 selected products unread; workspace-less Gateway announced complete | `readTenant` admits the overview plus one finite read per chosen product (Red Team statistics and scans; model scans, skill statistics and skill scans) as parts of one read; each settles into a per-source outcome (read / needs a role / failed) in `ReadStatus`; a chosen Gateway without a workspace is `incomplete` and named in `sourcesMissing`; `recheckProduct` re-reads one chosen product and refuses an unchosen one. Tests: `ui_v2_inbox::reads_cover_every_chosen_product_with_finite_per_source_outcomes` | `authority.rs`, `management_domain.rs` (`admit_read_part`), `observation_domain.rs`, `inbox_domain.rs` |
| R5 actions lost their target | `InboxEntry.target: InboxTarget{feature, product, resource, item}`; a key item opens Administration on API keys filtered to the key; setup warnings open where they are fixed (Settings, AI Gateway, AI Red Teaming). The shell hands the target to the destination (`arrival`), which selects it on mount or while open. Tests: `inbox.test` (Administration opens on API keys with the key filtered) | `inbox_domain.rs`, `inbox.tsx` (`follow`), `store.ts`, `feature-body.tsx`, `administration-view.tsx` |
| R6 action outcomes discarded | Home and Inbox actions (Read now, Recheck, Acknowledge, Snooze, Unsnooze) go through one `onAct` that reports a refusal (naming the tenant or item, with the refusal's text) or failed delivery as a warn toast and keeps an unconfirmed delivery inline with Retry (never replayed on its own); an admitted recheck announces the product. The palette's Read now is `readTenant`. Tests: `inbox.test` outcomes | `app.tsx` (`v2Act`), `home.tsx`, `inbox.tsx`, `copy.ts` |
| R7 snooze toast rediscovered old holds | The core issues `InboxView.lastSnooze` (`SnoozeReceipt{id, title, returnsAt, sequence}`); the shell announces a new sequence once in the tenant it was placed in, with its own baseline per effect (no shared tenant ref). Tests: `inbox.test` (a switch to a tenant with a hold and a reread announce nothing; a new receipt announces once) | `observation_domain.rs`, `inbox_domain.rs`, `v2-shell.tsx` |
| R8 Inbox columns clipped at 200% | The two columns are `repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 300px), 1fr))` with `min-w-0` and wrapping titles: they stack when both do not fit; native C30-N04 asserts rows, detail text, facts and every action inside the window at 900×600 and 200% in both themes | `inbox.tsx`, `acceptance_c30.py` |
